DESCRIPTION:Long Run 18km @ 6:30–6:45/km — keep firmly at the easy end 
 of the pace range the day after the 10K race effort\, cutting 2km to allow
  for residual fatigue.\n\nReason: Running a hard 10K on 8 November means t
 he following Sunday long run should be slightly reduced in distance and he
 ld at the easier end of the aerobic pace range to avoid compounding fatigu
 e with no wellness data to guide load decisions.\n\nAI coaching 2026-11-07
